Chocolate Doom 3.1.1 for Pyxis
Upstream: https://github.com/chocolate-doom/chocolate-doom.git
Revision: 410d96855b5df5410ff591a90efeafa889119224 (tag chocolate-doom-3.1.1)
Patches: 0001-pyxis-sdl2-static-target.patch, 0002-pyxis-platform.patch,
         0003-pyxis-software-scaling.patch

Chocolate Doom and the patched files remain under the GNU General Public
License, version 2 or later, in COPYING.md. The program links the Pyxis SDL2
port statically; SDL2's zlib licence is SDL2-LICENSE.txt. SDL2_mixer is also
linked statically, under SDL2_mixer-LICENSE.txt, with its selected profile
recorded in SDL2_mixer-PORT-NOTICE.

The build enables digital effects and Chocolate Doom's OPL music synthesizer
through SDL2_mixer. SDL2_mixer MIDI decoders and SDL2_net remain disabled:
General MIDI/GUS music and network play are unavailable. No game data,
instrument patches or sound fonts are included in this recipe.

The linked SDL2 software-video and fdlibm code also retain the BSD-3-Clause
notice in SDL2-yuv2rgb-LICENSE and Sun's permission grant in SDL2-fdlibm-NOTICE.
